  "id": "project-pieces",
  "after": "overview",
  "title": "The pieces of almost every PyTorch project.",
  "caption": "Data flows from top to bottom. The Dataset fetches one car at a time. The DataLoader shuffles (फेंटना, phentna) the cars and groups them into batches of 32. The model, an `nn.Module`, makes a guess for each batch. The training loop measures the loss and updates the weights, then goes back for the next batch. At the end, you save the model to Google Drive.",
  "alt": "A vertical chain of six boxes: your data (1,000 used-car rows in a CSV file), Dataset (len(ds) gives 1000, ds[5] gives car 5), DataLoader (batches of 32 cars in a new random order), Model (an nn.Module, pred = model(xb)), Training loop (loss, backward, step for every batch) and Save (torch.save to Google Drive). A curved arrow labelled next batch goes from the training loop back to the DataLoader. A note at the bottom says to move the model and each batch to the GPU: model.to(device) and xb = xb.to(device).",
